        <headline>Frost Advisory issued September 26 at 12:38PM PDT until September 27 at 9:00AM PDT by NWS Spokane WA</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Temperatures as low as 33 will result in frost formation.

* WHERE...Spokane, Rockford, Coeur d'Alene, Othello, Potlatch,
Ephrata, Oakesdale, Moses Lake, Genesee, Worley, Post Falls,
Rosalia, Pullman, Tekoa, Moscow, Harrington, Grand Coulee, Creston,
La Crosse, Uniontown, Cheney, Ritzville, Odessa, Wilbur, Fairfield,
Spokane Valley, Airway Heights, Coulee City, Quincy, Plummer,
Davenport, Colfax, and Hayden.

* WHEN...From midnight tonight to 9 AM PDT Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Frost could harm sensitive outdoor vegetation. Sensitive
outdoor plants may be killed if left uncovered.
</description>
        <instruction>Take steps now to protect tender plants from the cold.</instruction>
